        <div class="cw-footer">
          <div class="cw-name">Lev Marhabi — לֵב מַרְחַבִּי</div>
          <div class="cw-bio-text">The last Jew in Yemen. Arrested by Houthi forces in March 2016, accused of helping fellow Jews remove a Torah scroll from the country. Sentenced to prison in 2018. An appeals court ordered his release in 2019; Houthi security forces refused to comply. Has been held in solitary confinement and reported to be in poor health. No Yemeni Jewish community can advocate for him — they are gone. His family lives in exile. He remains.</div>
          <div class="cw-since">Arrested March 2016 · Last known member of a community over 2,500 years old · Yemeni Jewish population at independence (1962): ~50,000 · Today: 1</div>
